smartclockmon (0.6.10-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Stop polling the receiver's status screen.  It is 1574 bytes, about
    1.5 s of a 19200 link and four times what a whole one-second poll
    costs, and after the satellite counts moved to direct queries the
    only thing left on it that appears nowhere else is per-satellite
    elevation, azimuth and signal strength.  It is now read on request,
    by whoever is looking at a sky plot: a page at /sky in the browser
    and a view of its own in the monitor.
  * Run each poll tier a step at a time rather than as one pass, so a
    slow tier holds the link for its longest single query instead of
    for all of them.
  * Read the satellite counts with :GPS:SATellite:TRACking:COUNt? and
    :GPS:SATellite:VISible:PREDicted:COUNt? instead of scraping them,
    which is 0.16 s against 1.5 s.  The browser shows both as "7 of 9
    up".
  * Poll the medium tier every ten seconds rather than every thirty,
    now that it no longer carries the status screen.
  * Plot the Allan deviation of the 1 PPS against GPS, at /adev in the
    browser and in a view of its own in the monitor.  Runs are cut
    where a relock, a holdover or an absence makes the phase either
    side incomparable, and only the second differences that exist are
    counted, so a record with gaps in it is measured rather than
    misread.
  * Recognise 4800, 38400, 57600 and 115200 baud, so a receiver some
    other tool has moved to one can still be reached to move it back.
    The 58503A itself tops out at 19200: asked for 38400 it answers
    "No error" and keeps the rate it had.

