smartclockmon (0.6.3-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * The GPS week rollover is shown as the ordinary condition it is.
    Firmware predating the 2019 wrap reports a date 1024 weeks behind
    and nearly every receiver of this vintage does, so the clients now
    show the corrected date with the correction noted quietly, instead
    of a red WRONG in the monitor and a permanently lit warning in the
    browser strip.  A warning that is always on teaches you to ignore
    the place real faults appear.
  * What the receiver actually reported stays visible beside it.  The
    correction is arithmetic done by the daemon against the host clock,
    not something the instrument said, and a reader should be able to
    see which of the two is being trusted.
  * The corrected date is computed once by the daemon rather than by
    each client.  A client older than the daemon is unaffected; a page
    newer than its daemon says the date is as reported rather than
    claiming a correction it did not receive.
  * Fixed: a column that never changes got an axis built from floating
    point noise.  Averaging a constant per bucket does not return it
    exactly, so oven current held at 104.9 spanned 2e-14 and the axis
    read 104.900000000000020.  The learned tempco, which really is
    constant, would have done the same.

